ot of employees who  might be in more call them  administrative roles you know they might  be doing marketing for example or in  finance whatever it might be I mean it  really ranges but Tech recruiters have  been telling us that it's typically  those with technical Talent like  Engineers like data scientists are  probably a little safer than those who  might feel more corporate functions  I mean given how many people are losing  their jobs are there enough places for  them to go well the job market has  remained really tight this has been an  economy that has where a lot of  companies have been looking for  technical talent for a long time so  there are plenty of big companies that  still would like to hire from Big Tech  but we've heard from recruiters and  others that you know there may not be  enough startups for example that could  absorb all of these employees in the  market that it may be a little bit more  difficult and so I think it sort of  depends what happens over the next  couple of months but this is a job  market that is changing even though  plenty of places would be happy to add  additional Engineers would be happy to  have program managers and data  scientists and others in their companies  and so what I think this is doing is  causing some people in Tech to look  elsewhere for roles we've been hearing  that some are considering perhaps  industries that seem a little more  stable like financial services for  example or something like logistics  companies that may not have been on  people's radar before but now now might  be appealing in part because they still  offer High cash pay but they also maybe  offer a little more stability right now  workers are going to  feel being at the jobs because you  mentioned they might have equivalent pay  but the perks that was always a tech  thing yeah I mean the perks may be a  little bit different one company I spoke  with it's citizens Financial it's a  regional bank and the Chief Information  officer there told me that you know we  offer stability we offer meaningful work  we have interesting projects we do not  offer ping pong tables or Nitro cold  brew so there'd be an adjustment there  and but I think people throughout the  pandemic have reassessed their careers  what they want from them and they want  oftentimes more flexibility they want  careers they can feel good about so this  is all coming at an interesting time  we'll have to see sort of how workers  decide where to go next as they sort of  assess what's happening in Tech right  now and where they want to go people  aren't just jumping in for the Nitro  cold brew anymore I guess as nice as  that is as much as everybody loves cold  brew it's uh there's maybe more to  consider I mean let's talk a little bit  more about that mood obviously layoffs  don't make anyone happy but what kind of  reactions are we seeing from the people  who are losing their jobs well there's  real sadness out there I mean you see  this in Anonymous posts on the network  blind people just saying this is just  the start of what might be more to come  you see on social media networks like  LinkedIn people offering help to those  who've been laid off there have been  layoff lists distributed so a lot of  people are trying to help in this moment  and recruiters say they've also noticed  a shift where recruiters who for years  were trying to get on the radar of tech  Talent were trying to convince them to  be you know interested in certain  opportunities they now say that they're  seeing a real Spike an inbound requests  from Tech workers what about the mood of  the people who aren't being let go and  are still at these big Tech companies  well that's always a real issue I mean  it's those who remain sometimes feel  that sort of survivor's guilt where they  now are forced to manage teams or  operate within teams that have fewer  people perhaps there's questions about  why some were laid off and others remain  it can take a real toll on morale inside  companies and I think that's a real  issue that managers and Executives and  others will have to think through  because after a layoff like projects do  change projects might have to be  redistributed to other workers it's all  a lot to take in and you've seen that  already after a number of the big  layoffs where workers are just saying it  feels sad inside some of these companies  what about those perks for the people  who remain at the big tech companies I  mean the Nitro cold brew the free  laundry are these things still  incentivizing them to stay at the big  tech companies well I think a lot of  tech workers would say you know they're  at these companies primarily because  they feel like they're doing interesting  work and they feel like they're doing  projects that help them grow and of  course they are compensated for that  depend a and the stock all of that is  typically above what they might make in  other Industries and so I think a lot of  people want to remain in tech for these  reasons I think many are then just  trying to figure out where in Tech makes  sense are there places where you could  sort of work for the moment that feel a  little more stable than others  how are those being affected by the  layoffs tech stocks are way down  people's net worth is tied up in the  equity that they have in their company  and so a lot of tech workers have said  they now are reassessing whether they  want to take vacations whether they want  to perhaps sell a car whatever it might  mean so this does have an effect and  what's interesting too is that some  Venture Capital firms are advising  employers to try to conserve cash as  much as possible and so that might mean  not raising salaries as much in the  future or trying to kind of keep pay  flat I think there are real questions  about how people sort of fare in all  this all right that's our reporter chip  cutter thanks for joining us chip you're  welcome thanks for having me and that's  it for today's Tech news briefing if you  want more Tech stories check out our  website I'm Zoe Thomas for The Wall  Street Journal thanks for listening  [Music]  [Music]

